{"title":"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Ishan_Also_See\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Ishan Also See</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the area enclosed by the geoboard quadrilateral below?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/0/76034624e12f53431e5b0c0d4dd5abb475dc1fbb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(3mm); defaultpen(linewidth(.8pt)); dotfactor=2;  for(int a=0; a&lt;=10; ++a) for(int b=0; b&lt;=10; ++b)  {   dot((a,b));  };  draw((4,0)--(0,5)--(3,4)--(10,10)--cycle); [/asy]\" width=\"145\" height=\"145\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/a/1ea1f7dd314c3674ffcf91f17f6b7e89cf32d6c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 15\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 18\\frac12 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 22\\frac12 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 27 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 41$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"419\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/5/005f9f59d2c18f343506c5ccec951cf72f6aa5aa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(5mm); defaultpen(linewidth(.8pt)); dotfactor=2;  for(int a=0; a&lt;=10; ++a) for(int b=0; b&lt;=10; ++b)  {   dot((a,b));  };  draw((4,0)--(0,5)--(3,4)--(10,10)--cycle); draw((0,0)--(10,0)--(10,10)--(3,4)--(0,5)--cycle); draw((10,4)--(0,4)--cycle);  dot(&quot;$A$&quot;, (0,5), W); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;, (3,4), N); dot(&quot;$C$&quot;, (10,10), NE); dot(&quot;$D$&quot;, (0,4), W); dot(&quot;$E$&quot;, (10,4), E); dot(&quot;$F$&quot;, (0,0), SW); dot(&quot;$G$&quot;, (10,0), SE); dot(&quot;$H$&quot;, (4,0), S); [/asy]\" width=\"288\" height=\"282\" />\n</p><p>Divide the shape up as above. \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/1/451699e68db782227a57cee6b41a225de3111d0b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[Area = [DEGF] + [ABD] + [BCE] - [AFH] - [CGH] = 4 \\cdot 10 + \\frac12 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 3 + \\frac12 \\cdot 7 \\cdot 6 - \\frac12 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 4 - \\frac12 \\cdot 6 \\cdot 10 = 40 + \\frac32 + 21 - 10 - 30 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 22\\frac12}\\]\" width=\"962\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Isabelchen\">isabelchen</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the bottom left corner be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />. The points would then be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/6/aa653c09e6a09ab2db79a85a76b7415a721cc8e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4,0),(0,5),(3,4),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/0/9404bda8b5bf203a7a1786f2358d0fb7cd359bd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(10,10)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" />. Applying the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Shoelace_Theorem\" title=\"Shoelace Theorem\">Shoelace Theorem</a>,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/f/aef8fe6ea9b1a051bd78f12eb4ba437eb8173f61.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{Area} = \\frac12 \\begin{vmatrix} 4 &amp; 0 \\\\ 0 &amp; 5 \\\\ 3 &amp; 4 \\\\ 10 &amp; 10 \\\\ 4 &amp; 0\\end{vmatrix} = \\frac12 |(20+30)-(15+40+40)| = \\frac12 |50-95| = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 22\\frac12}\\]\" width=\"561\" height=\"97\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The figure contains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25d31faf472ddb4c698a14522fe8125c06f8dd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> interior points and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> boundary points. Using <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pick%27s_Theorem\" title=\"Pick&#39;s Theorem\">Pick's Theorem</a>, the area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/e/f5e1586abbf61db3a45123dd45f1f2b1c1d8c6bd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[21+\\frac{5}{2}-1=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 22\\frac12}\\]\" width=\"185\" height=\"48\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Ishan_Also_See\">Ishan Also See</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Ishan Also See\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8\" title=\"2004 AMC 8\">2004 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2004\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Pr